"A Counterexample to the Antipodal Colouring Conjecture for Great-Pseudocircle Arrangements | Zenodo (https://zenodo.org/records/22969049)\nciteturn2search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; Crawled: last month; # A Counterexample to the Antipodal Colouring Conjecture for Great-Pseudocircle Arrangements ... We also certify a witness consisting of 26 actual great circles, using rational coefficients derived from published coordinate data of Parpalak and Utkin. ... Coloring circle arrangements: New 4-chromatic planar graphs. ... Preprint arXiv:2205.08181 (2022).\nPublished September 26, 2026 | Version 1\n\nPreprint Open\n\n# A Counterexample to the Antipodal Colouring Conjecture for Great-Pseudocircle Arrangements\n\n### Authors/Creators\n\n  * Seamons, John\n\n## Description\n\nWe observe that the triangle–pentagon structure of a projective pseudoline arrangement constructed by Blanc rules out an antipodal proper 3-colouring of its spherical lift. The projective graph has 325 vertices, and 215 triangles together with one pentagon cover every vertex twice. Hence every independent set has at most 108 vertices, which excludes a 3-colouring. This disproves the antipodal-colouring conjecture of Chiu et al. We also certify a witness consisting of 26 actual great circles, using rational coefficients derived from published coordinate data of Parpalak and Utkin. A small, self-contained Python package checks the geometry and the counting certificate exactly. The ordinary spherical graph of this witness does admit a proper 3-colouring.\n\n### \n\nantipodal_colouring_counterexample_v2.pdf\n\nPreview\n\n### \n\nFiles (1.5 MB)\n\nName  | Size  | Download all\n--- | --- | ---\nantipodal_26_verification_v1.zip md5:ecd0ed625e33d683eb4a1ce50a4eed46  | 6.2 kB  | Preview Download\nantipodal_colouring_counterexample_v2.pdf md5:83629770bc8b4501ba36c41ab15a1abf  | 1.4 MB  | Preview Download\n\n## Additional details\n\n### Additional titles\n\nSubtitle (English)\n    A Colouring Cons